        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by the incorrect handling of user authorizations, specifically in the way they were being sorted and displayed. The original implementation used a `SortedSet`, which may not have provided the desired case-insensitive sorting or could have introduced complexity in managing the authorization data. This could lead to incorrect or unexpected output when displaying authorizations to the user.

        Commit message:
        ACCUMULO-3784 fix getauths

Signed-off-by: Josh Elser <elserj@apache.org>  

        Patch:

